+
+# SPEC: parse_duration rejects trailing text
+
+## 🎯 Intent
+`parse_duration` in `timeparse/parse.py` scans with `finditer`, so anything after the last
+matched `<digits><unit>` token is silently dropped (`"1h30m5"` returns 5400). A user reported it;
+invalid input must raise `ValueError`.
+
+## 🌅 Outcomes
+Any input with unconsumed text after the last unit raises `ValueError`. All currently accepted
+inputs return the same values as before.
+
+## 📋 In-Scope Scenarios
+
+### S1: Trailing text is rejected
+**Given** a string whose valid duration prefix is followed by extra text
+**When** `parse_duration` is called with `"1h30m5"`, `"1h30m!"`, `"2d junk"` or `"45sx"`
+**Then** each call raises `ValueError`
+
+### S2: Existing valid behaviour is unchanged
+**Given** valid duration strings
+**When** `parse_duration` is called with `" 1h30m "`, `"1H30M"`, `"0s"` or `"100000s"`
+**Then** it returns 5400, 5400, 0 and 100000 respectively
+
+### S3: Leading and interior junk still rejected
+**Given** text before or between units
+**When** `parse_duration` is called with `"x1h"` or `"1h 30m"`
+**Then** each call raises `ValueError`
+
+## 🚫 Non-Goals
+- No change to the unit table, ordering rule, or error message wording.
+- No change to `format_duration` or `cli.py`.
+
+## ⚠️ Constraints
+| Constraint | Value | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Test framework | `pytest` | existing `tests/test_parse.py` |
+| Compatibility | public signature `parse_duration(str) -> int` unchanged | callers in `cli.py`, `__init__.py` |
+
+## 🔒 Irreversible Decisions
+none
+
+## ✅ Verification Criteria
+| Scenario | Verification mode | Test name / manual step |
+|---|---|---|
+| S1 | unit | `tests/test_parse.py::test_invalid` (add the four inputs) |
+| S2 | unit | `tests/test_parse.py::test_valid` (existing rows must stay green) |
+| S3 | unit | `tests/test_parse.py::test_invalid` |
+
+Oracle: golden — the expected values are quoted verbatim from the user's report and the documented behaviours; independent of the implementation.
+
+## ❓ Open Questions
+none
+
+## 🔍 Refinement Decisions
+- Skipped interview — single file, acceptance fully enumerated by the report, no API/format change, trivially reversible. `lane: light`, `irreversible_decisions: []`, stamped exempt.
+- `spec-validator` not dispatched (skip path, empty irreversible list).
